Package: titraR
Type: Package
Title: Titra — Interactive DBS Programming & Electrophysiology DAG Studio (htmlwidget & Shiny)
Version: 1.0.0
Authors@R: person("Titra", "Team", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "titra@example.org")
Description: R htmlwidget and interactive Shiny studio port of the Titra AnyWidget for
    deep brain stimulation (DBS) programming and electrophysiology. Detects, verifies,
    normalizes, and merges Medtronic Percept JSON session reports and amplitude-titration
    exports entirely in native R; computes Welch PSD, STFT spectrograms, beta and dynamic
    f_stim/2 finely-tuned gamma (FTG) dynamics, game-theoretic equilibria, extreme-value
    tail risk (CVaR/EVT-VaR/POT/GEV), log-OU option-pricing adaptivity lattices, and
    graph signal processing (GSP) amplitude-state biomarkers. Renders the full reactive
    Titra DAG canvas (Welcome screen, 4-stage progress bar, 17 curated presets, custom
    pipeline builder, compact FTG controller, multi-format reports, and instant Clear)
    inside RStudio Viewer, Quarto/R Markdown, or a full-screen Shiny web application.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
LazyData: false
Depends:
    R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports:
